# Steeler Voices — the knobs for `make dev`. Copy to `.env` (git-ignored) and
# edit; every line is optional. Nothing here is a secret: the platform runs
# with no keys. Each service's own variables are committed beside it in
# `<service>/.env.development` (dev values, nothing secret) and are read by
# compose automatically.

# Where the model runs. The default is the host's Ollama (Docker reaches it at
# host.docker.internal). Point it at a remote Ollama — the optional GPU rig,
# `infra/rig/` — to make tagging and generation fast.
#OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434

# No Ollama on this machine? Run it in a container (CPU only, slower).
#COMPOSE_PROFILES=bundled-ollama

# The only credential in the platform, and only for the optional rig (RunPod).
# It can live here or in ~/.config/steeler-voices/rig.env.
#RUNPOD_API_KEY=
